eola be tighter was  by far at least variable in these  samples and a clear difference could be  seen between the treatments even though  I've sampled approximately the same  number of plants as before so with this  in mind I set out to do this experiment  one more time this time I took PDL  simples and I also tripled the number of  plants in each treatment because I  really was tired of doing this  experiment  so here you can see that silencing a go  one significantly increased feeler be  tighter relative to the control plants  you can also see that PRD tighter was  significantly more variable in the a go  one silenced plants than in the controls  you might remember that we saw this in  the very first set of experiments I did  too I also checked trv tighter you can  see that silencing a go one also clearly  increased steel RV RV tighter which  makes sense given that a go one has role  in general antiviral defense however  unlike PLR be trv tighter was similarly  variable in the control and a go one  silenced plants this suggests to me that  there's something unique about the  relationship between pol RV and a go one  beyond a go one's role in broad-spectrum  virus defense although I was incredibly  happy to see some low key values after  all of that optimization I've actually  saved what I think is the most  interesting result for last it's a  little bit hard to see in this photo but  infection with trv a go one alone that  is without pilar be present causes some  stunting and morphological defects this  isn't really surprising because a go one  is known to have a role in  transcriptional regulation during  development that said these plants are  still very much alive and will even  eventually flower pilar the infection on  the other hand causes very mild symptoms  even when our control version of trv is  present however if you combine TR v a go  one and Pilar V infection the plant  withers away and eventually dies to  understand why this might occur we need  to th